WEBVTT

01:04.064 --> 01:05.982
WHEN LIFE GIVES YOU TANGERINES

01:09.527 --> 01:12.238
Six out of ten boats in Dodong-ri
belong to the Bu family.

01:13.073 --> 01:15.950
Eight out of ten people
have connections with them.

01:16.034 --> 01:17.619
Who's going to hire Gwan-sik?

01:19.329 --> 01:20.580
That guy is no good,

01:20.663 --> 01:23.500
but his older brother,
the chief of the fishing co-op,

01:23.583 --> 01:25.126
is acting up even more.

01:26.377 --> 01:29.881
Island folk don't take kindly
to newcomers. He just got unlucky.

01:31.508 --> 01:32.717
What the…

01:35.220 --> 01:36.221
What happened?

01:37.430 --> 01:38.681
They sent you away again?

01:39.641 --> 01:40.767
Bad economy, apparently.

01:41.351 --> 01:43.895
What, so people won't eat fish
'cause the economy is bad?

01:43.978 --> 01:45.105
Go home!

01:45.772 --> 01:46.773
Hey.

01:48.983 --> 01:51.694
I hear they're building a road
around Hallasan.

01:52.362 --> 01:53.947
Tell him to find a job there.

01:54.030 --> 01:56.533
Money is money,
whether it's from the sea or manual labor.

01:58.827 --> 02:01.496
Freshly picked by haenyeo!
Top-quality conch!

02:01.579 --> 02:04.749
The conches are top-quality today.
So are the sea squirts.

02:06.126 --> 02:09.295
I hear he's the first to arrive
every morning,

02:09.379 --> 02:11.256
lining up early to get work.

02:11.881 --> 02:15.426
Gwan-sik is always the first in line
among the workers.

02:16.261 --> 02:17.262
It's so annoying.

02:18.054 --> 02:20.390
Why does he have to be so diligent?

02:20.473 --> 02:22.308
So, how's work for him?

02:22.392 --> 02:24.227
Is he okay with working on land now?

02:25.812 --> 02:28.064
He never says much.

02:28.148 --> 02:29.899
Of course he doesn't like it.

02:30.692 --> 02:32.944
A boatman will always yearn for the sea.

02:39.993 --> 02:40.827
Oh dear.

02:41.452 --> 02:43.580
My goodness. What now?

02:44.080 --> 02:45.874
What's wrong with your arm?

02:47.709 --> 02:49.544
I guess everything takes some skill.

02:51.671 --> 02:53.423
Did they tell you not to come back?

02:55.091 --> 02:56.301
Oh my.

02:59.554 --> 03:01.890
Why did he fix a perfectly good roof?

03:13.026 --> 03:14.819
Just get some rest, please.

03:16.404 --> 03:18.072
He was withering away.

03:22.243 --> 03:26.039
A hard-working cow was withering away
because it couldn't work.

03:28.750 --> 03:31.961
Good gracious.
He already assembled them all.

03:32.045 --> 03:34.756
I had three days to work on them.

03:37.133 --> 03:40.887
Mom said the leftover cabbages
she picked up in the field

03:41.763 --> 03:44.724
looked less withered
than the back of Dad's head then.

03:47.644 --> 03:50.647
DODONG-RI VARIETY SHOP

04:14.337 --> 04:16.881
Go back to sleep.
I've already started cooking the rice.

04:19.759 --> 04:23.012
You can take it easy. Just take it easy.

04:26.349 --> 04:27.600
Are you a cow?

04:28.977 --> 04:30.979
You've been selling fish
since you were nine.

04:31.062 --> 04:32.814
It's okay to take a break.

04:34.565 --> 04:36.567
Just think of it as a school holiday.

04:38.069 --> 04:39.320
I've never taken a break.

04:41.614 --> 04:42.782
It feels strange.

04:44.534 --> 04:45.368
Really strange.

04:46.703 --> 04:49.580
Come on, just enjoy yourself.

04:49.664 --> 04:51.874
You deserve some time off.

04:52.458 --> 04:55.753
If I enjoy myself,
how will the four of us get by?

04:59.465 --> 05:03.803
If I work for a day,
we'll make it through another day.

05:05.972 --> 05:07.223
But to work a day…

05:09.642 --> 05:10.852
It's just so unfair.

05:15.606 --> 05:17.859
Why worry about starving?

05:19.110 --> 05:21.946
I'll make the money if I need to.

05:26.784 --> 05:31.331
The Literary Girl who couldn't even say,
"These cabbages are sweet"?

05:49.515 --> 05:51.684
Standing before the cruel rice jar,

05:52.310 --> 05:56.314
Mom remembered her mother's smiling face.

06:00.360 --> 06:02.320
She remembered how her mother

06:03.029 --> 06:06.449
would put on a smile
just to sell another conch.

06:07.867 --> 06:10.286
So I was just wondering…

06:10.912 --> 06:11.788
I mean…

06:13.414 --> 06:14.248
Some rice--

06:14.332 --> 06:16.876
I don't understand what you're saying.

06:18.920 --> 06:20.213
Stop whining.

06:20.963 --> 06:22.548
There are many worse off than you.

06:29.555 --> 06:32.892
The same way I've never forgotten
the look on her young face

06:33.518 --> 06:35.812
as she struggled to smile through it.

06:38.898 --> 06:41.234
Your dad gets ripped off wherever he goes.

06:41.734 --> 06:43.903
We saved 1,000 won per box.

06:44.695 --> 06:48.199
I can't believe you asked for a discount.
You're such a mom.

06:50.701 --> 06:51.577
Are you happy?

06:52.328 --> 06:53.329
It's funny.

06:54.288 --> 06:58.251
When I was younger, I couldn't even say,
"These cabbages are sweet."

06:58.334 --> 06:59.168
You? Seriously?

06:59.961 --> 07:02.213
I was such a shy Literary Girl.

07:03.464 --> 07:06.509
I was so embarrassed to sell cabbages
in my school uniform

07:07.093 --> 07:11.013
that I'd bury my face in books like this.

07:11.097 --> 07:12.974
So what happened to you?

07:14.767 --> 07:19.272
Over time, I learned there are
worse things that truly hurt your pride,

07:20.857 --> 07:22.900
like living in a one-bedroom house

07:22.984 --> 07:25.653
and having to ignore the sound
of your family's stomachs

07:26.154 --> 07:28.448
growling with hunger all night.

07:30.199 --> 07:32.702
That was a true embarrassment.

07:36.080 --> 07:39.083
Back then, everything was new to me.

07:40.168 --> 07:43.463
For some reason,
it all felt so humiliating and pathetic.

07:45.256 --> 07:48.301
There were so many times
when I felt like I couldn't go on.

07:48.968 --> 07:50.636
Say something, will you?

07:50.720 --> 07:52.763
What good will come
of you not speaking up?

07:53.931 --> 07:56.392
Why bring your pride
when you're here to borrow money?

07:56.476 --> 07:59.228
If you can't say a word,
why did you bother showing up?

08:01.856 --> 08:02.773
What is it?

08:02.857 --> 08:04.275
Is something bothering you?

08:05.067 --> 08:05.902
Ae-sun,

08:06.527 --> 08:08.946
you honor their ancestors now, not ours.

08:09.614 --> 08:11.491
You should ask his family for help.

08:11.574 --> 08:14.035
Why is Yang's wife causing a scene here?

08:14.827 --> 08:16.829
I thought you were resourceful
like your mom,

08:16.913 --> 08:19.165
but you're also as bad with words
as your dad was.

08:19.749 --> 08:20.833
Is there no other way?

08:21.751 --> 08:24.712
What if there isn't?
Is there even any land left to sell?

08:27.256 --> 08:31.344
You must really be desperate to come here,
but we're drowning in debt ourselves!

08:39.977 --> 08:42.230
Damn, Ae-sun.
Why can't you just be doing well?

08:43.814 --> 08:45.316
Give her that ring if you want.

08:55.034 --> 08:58.955
No rice in the jar to feed your kid,
and you can't bring yourself to speak?

09:04.293 --> 09:06.003
You are still such a baby.

09:16.722 --> 09:17.557
Honey.

09:19.058 --> 09:19.892
Yes?

09:21.727 --> 09:22.937
I just want to

09:24.814 --> 09:26.816
grow old fast.

09:30.403 --> 09:31.237
Why?

09:31.862 --> 09:32.697
Just because.

09:34.448 --> 09:37.243
I thought once everyone became adults,

09:38.035 --> 09:41.414
they'd be able to carry hot bowls
with their bare hands, just like my mom.

09:42.957 --> 09:47.169
I thought they'd become like Gyeong-ja,
who just eats without a worry,

09:48.337 --> 09:50.464
even when creditors invade their home.

09:54.760 --> 09:56.804
I thought that once you grew up…

09:59.181 --> 10:02.310
your hands and heart
would naturally become calloused.

10:06.397 --> 10:08.357
But everything's still too hot for me.

10:11.068 --> 10:12.445
I get burned every day,

10:13.529 --> 10:14.739
but it hurts every time.

10:16.657 --> 10:18.701
Am I the only fool in the world?

10:18.784 --> 10:19.827
Is everyone else

10:20.620 --> 10:22.455
adulting just fine?

10:24.832 --> 10:26.167
They all just pretend

10:27.335 --> 10:32.006
to be adults
because people tell them they are adults.

10:36.802 --> 10:40.014
I just want to grow old fast.

10:43.142 --> 10:44.268
Maybe it's because

10:45.895 --> 10:49.815
it's my first time
being a mom, a wife, and an adult.

10:51.317 --> 10:53.069
I don't know why…

10:55.738 --> 10:57.657
everything is so tough and overwhelming.

11:19.053 --> 11:19.887
Hold me.

11:25.935 --> 11:26.977
Pat my back.

11:38.114 --> 11:43.369
Sleep, sleep, rock to sleep

11:43.994 --> 11:48.749
Sleep, sleep, rock to sleep

11:49.792 --> 11:55.131
My baby sleeps well

11:56.507 --> 12:01.846
Sleep, sleep, rock to sleep

12:02.555 --> 12:05.474
Sleep, sleep…

12:05.975 --> 12:06.809
Sun.

12:09.729 --> 12:10.604
Ae-sun.

12:20.781 --> 12:23.993
Did you lose sleep
because you didn't give me the ring?

12:33.043 --> 12:35.337
Don't dig so deeply.

12:35.421 --> 12:36.881
My husband's right there.

12:39.675 --> 12:41.302
Don't even take it out.

12:41.385 --> 12:44.805
I wouldn't be able to sleep if you gave us
the money you have stashed away.

12:45.598 --> 12:47.391
-Buy a boat.
-Buy what?

12:48.434 --> 12:50.352
Buy a boat, and don't say a word.

12:50.853 --> 12:53.272
If anyone asks, say you won the lottery.

13:02.406 --> 13:04.074
-Did you steal this?
-It's my money.

13:04.158 --> 13:07.703
It's the money I made
from selling gukbap before the war.

13:09.580 --> 13:11.791
You've been holding onto this
the entire time?

13:11.874 --> 13:15.211
Jong-gu is a bottomless pit.
He would've gambled it all away.

13:16.879 --> 13:18.756
So you hid it to give it to me?

13:18.839 --> 13:23.010
Your mom threatened me.
She said this would make us even.

13:23.719 --> 13:24.553
What?

13:28.015 --> 13:29.391
Please, God, she must live on.

13:30.392 --> 13:32.520
How could you take her away from her kids?

13:35.314 --> 13:36.315
Mother.

13:40.402 --> 13:41.570
Mother.

13:48.536 --> 13:50.371
Could you please come with me?

13:51.914 --> 13:53.249
I'm scared to go on my own.

13:53.749 --> 13:55.543
FOREVER YOUNG STUDIO

14:01.257 --> 14:03.968
Didn't I buy this for you
when you got married?

14:06.303 --> 14:09.181
This is my best outfit.

14:13.602 --> 14:16.480
I think it's because
we risk our lives at work

14:17.940 --> 14:20.442
that we haenyeo believe
in so many superstitions.

14:21.068 --> 14:22.611
They say when we take photos,

14:23.112 --> 14:25.364
they will soon be used for our funerals.

14:27.533 --> 14:30.452
I've had a coffin on my back
for my whole life,

14:31.537 --> 14:33.497
but I still fear death,

14:33.581 --> 14:35.708
and that's why
I never had my picture taken.

14:35.791 --> 14:36.876
Look at me.

14:48.804 --> 14:51.515
Your children will remember you
by this photo.

14:52.975 --> 14:54.643
Pink will look great on you.

14:58.272 --> 15:00.107
Let's take one for your funeral

15:00.774 --> 15:02.401
and one for mine.

15:05.195 --> 15:06.447
You need to live longer.

15:07.615 --> 15:08.574
Join me later.

15:14.538 --> 15:16.040
I've outlived my child

15:17.833 --> 15:19.209
for far too long.

15:20.669 --> 15:22.463
Even after losing my precious child,

15:22.963 --> 15:26.592
my life just went on,
still eating three meals a day.

15:32.139 --> 15:33.349
I'll make sure

15:34.350 --> 15:35.559
I find your precious son.

15:39.313 --> 15:41.482
I'll stay by his side in the afterlife

15:42.691 --> 15:44.360
instead of finding a new husband.

15:46.946 --> 15:48.781
If you see Han-gyu before I do…

15:50.950 --> 15:52.242
tell him I'm sorry.

15:55.371 --> 15:56.956
Tell him Mom is sorry.

15:58.916 --> 16:00.167
Please tell him that.

16:01.335 --> 16:02.169
Please…

16:11.178 --> 16:13.597
I'll make sure he gets the message,

16:14.974 --> 16:16.225
so please stay here

16:17.142 --> 16:18.978
and look after Han-gyu's child.

16:20.604 --> 16:21.772
Take care of Ae-sun

16:23.023 --> 16:24.775
as you would've taken care of Han-gyu.

16:28.904 --> 16:29.989
I thought so.

16:31.865 --> 16:34.159
You brought me here to tell me that.

16:34.910 --> 16:36.870
How else would you rest in peace?

16:40.040 --> 16:41.500
She'll be an orphan

16:42.835 --> 16:44.169
at just ten years old.

16:45.796 --> 16:48.007
She just needs one person to rely on.

16:52.219 --> 16:54.346
It's all my misfortune.

16:55.139 --> 16:56.265
It's all my fault.

16:57.683 --> 16:59.560
She's not without shame.

17:00.519 --> 17:02.146
She won't bother you all the time.

17:03.147 --> 17:04.898
If the day comes

17:05.482 --> 17:08.694
when that shy girl comes looking
for her grandmother's help…

17:11.030 --> 17:13.115
then her life must be unbearably hard…

17:15.743 --> 17:17.327
so please help her out once.

17:21.832 --> 17:23.500
She can weather even the worst

17:24.710 --> 17:26.045
without saying a word.

17:29.631 --> 17:30.883
But if she ever says…

17:32.926 --> 17:35.012
"Grandma, I'm struggling,
and I need help…"

17:35.512 --> 17:36.680
if ever she says that,

17:38.140 --> 17:40.225
please save her
like you'd save your own son.

17:42.269 --> 17:44.271
Just once. No more, no less.

17:45.731 --> 17:47.066
Please help her just once.

17:49.151 --> 17:50.861
Then everything will be even.

17:51.445 --> 17:53.989
You'll have nothing to apologize for
to Ae-sun's father.

17:55.365 --> 17:56.241
Gwang-rye,

17:56.325 --> 17:58.368
Ae-sun is my grandchild.

17:58.452 --> 18:01.789
Why worry about her
when you have a long journey ahead?

18:03.499 --> 18:04.875
I just can't go yet.

18:06.543 --> 18:07.461
I just can't.

18:09.296 --> 18:10.130
Dear.

18:13.717 --> 18:15.010
You can go in peace.

18:16.261 --> 18:17.805
Leave your worries behind.

18:43.914 --> 18:44.790
Here we go.

18:45.415 --> 18:47.376
One, two, three.

19:04.351 --> 19:05.310
Grandma.

19:07.771 --> 19:10.774
Will I miss my mom less
when I become a grandmother?

19:12.943 --> 19:14.361
Of course not.

19:17.072 --> 19:19.575
The pain of losing a parent
cuts deeper as life goes on,

19:20.075 --> 19:25.080
but the pain of losing a child is etched
in the deepest part of your heart.

19:26.165 --> 19:28.458
When a parent dies,
you send them to heaven.

19:29.042 --> 19:30.460
But when a child dies,

19:32.129 --> 19:33.797
you keep them alive in here.

19:35.799 --> 19:39.469
You can't let them go,
so you keep them alive in here.

19:43.515 --> 19:45.309
So just take it quickly.

19:46.310 --> 19:48.520
Giving it to you
is like giving it to my son.

19:57.905 --> 19:59.114
I'll make you proud.

20:00.574 --> 20:02.659
I'll make sure to live a good life.

20:09.291 --> 20:10.292
We'll make you proud.

20:12.586 --> 20:14.087
That's all I want.

20:25.307 --> 20:30.729
A MIDSUMMER NIGHT'S FULL NETS

20:33.565 --> 20:35.943
Our dear Captain Yang.

20:37.778 --> 20:41.865
I hope every day is this good!

20:43.784 --> 20:48.789
Captain Yang. This is great. I'm so happy.

20:53.460 --> 20:54.461
There we are.

20:54.544 --> 20:57.881
What a beautiful day!
This is the best day!

21:22.864 --> 21:23.824
Dragon King,

21:24.658 --> 21:27.160
May the ship not follow the fish,

21:27.244 --> 21:29.329
but the fish follow the ship.

21:30.372 --> 21:32.332
May its nets always be full!

21:32.416 --> 21:35.168
May its nets always be full!

21:35.919 --> 21:38.297
Please!

21:44.428 --> 21:45.262
Bless us.

21:46.221 --> 21:48.932
It's a boat as long as it floats.

21:49.016 --> 21:51.351
Have some makgeolli at Captain Yang's!

21:51.435 --> 21:52.644
You sure it will float?

21:53.937 --> 21:56.106
Why is she making such a fuss?

22:01.153 --> 22:02.654
Captain Yang!

22:02.738 --> 22:04.072
Captain Yang!

22:04.156 --> 22:06.116
Captain Yang!

22:06.199 --> 22:08.160
Captain Yang!

22:08.243 --> 22:14.333
The fortune teller said he was born
with a bounty of food in each hand.

22:14.416 --> 22:18.337
Now he has set the Yangs' boat afloat
in the waters of Jeju!

22:22.382 --> 22:26.928
Captain Yang

22:27.012 --> 22:29.848
Captain Yang!

22:33.101 --> 22:34.227
What are you looking at?

22:34.311 --> 22:36.355
You can't hide the sky with your hand.

22:36.438 --> 22:38.982
You found Jong-gu, right?
You're in touch with him?

22:39.066 --> 22:40.609
You think I don't know you?

22:41.443 --> 22:42.527
Go tell him

22:42.611 --> 22:46.656
that I, Kim Chun-ok,
will report my own grandson for robbery.

22:47.282 --> 22:49.659
Jong-gu is still the eldest grandson.

22:49.743 --> 22:53.580
He will take care of your ancestral rites
and restore our family's fortune.

22:53.663 --> 22:54.706
Ae-sun

22:56.500 --> 22:58.126
is my eldest son's daughter.

22:58.210 --> 22:59.586
Captain Yang

22:59.669 --> 23:02.172
How great! Way to go!

23:02.255 --> 23:05.550
The sole male heir of the family,
born to Kwon Gye-ok,

23:05.634 --> 23:09.888
has set the Yangs' boat afloat
in the waters of Jeju!

23:13.975 --> 23:16.603
It's actually the Ohs' boat,
not the Yangs'.

23:17.854 --> 23:21.441
My grandmother bought me this boat.

23:22.359 --> 23:26.947
I must have been the bounty of food
in Gwan-sik's fortune!

23:29.533 --> 23:32.536
All right, you're such a blessing.

23:33.537 --> 23:35.080
The most blessed of all, she is!

23:35.163 --> 23:37.332
What should you do, then?

23:37.416 --> 23:39.459
You should treat her like a crown!

23:40.168 --> 23:43.839
She didn't even bring the silver spoon
you love so much,

23:44.339 --> 23:48.051
but now she's given you a boat!

23:48.552 --> 23:49.636
How wonderful!

23:50.679 --> 23:52.681
What a devoted daughter-in-law!

23:53.181 --> 23:55.725
The most devoted of all!

23:58.270 --> 24:00.605
Who bought him a boat? Who?

24:03.024 --> 24:04.401
You love her that much?

24:07.487 --> 24:08.572
Father.

24:08.655 --> 24:09.489
I think

24:10.615 --> 24:12.784
she's the funniest person in the world.

24:14.077 --> 24:18.039
Oh Ae-sun!

24:18.123 --> 24:21.585
There they stood that season,
like tall, green trees.

24:23.086 --> 24:26.840
It was the start of a summer
that could never be forgotten.

24:31.428 --> 24:32.929
Mom, you're peeing.

24:34.097 --> 24:34.931
Oh no.

24:35.891 --> 24:37.893
-It's too early.
-Ae-sun.

24:39.186 --> 24:42.230
Honey!

24:42.898 --> 24:45.817
Honey!

24:53.116 --> 24:53.950
Be careful!

25:14.387 --> 25:16.348
See what happens when you laugh out loud?

25:16.431 --> 25:18.558
This is what you get for cracking up!

25:19.434 --> 25:22.229
What did you do at my age?
What was your life like?

25:23.355 --> 25:24.189
I don't know.

25:24.689 --> 25:27.275
I think I was always pregnant.

25:40.247 --> 25:43.917
Gwan-sik made this, didn't he?
Wow, he's a master at it.

25:44.000 --> 25:46.461
He's so good at making jeon now.

25:51.716 --> 25:53.635
You like silver spoons.

25:54.177 --> 25:57.722
You must be so happy to have some.

26:00.058 --> 26:03.770
He made all these kinds of jeon
for his ancestors.

26:03.853 --> 26:07.315
What a devoted grandson.
No one could be more devoted than he is.

26:08.650 --> 26:11.903
Are you really not going to come
to the ancestral rites?

26:12.946 --> 26:15.323
-I can't change his mind, can I?
-You can't?

26:15.407 --> 26:20.870
I would love to go, but what can I do?
I should listen to my husband.

26:21.454 --> 26:25.458
He uses his death stare to warn me
not to go anywhere near your house.

26:25.542 --> 26:27.002
Oh, he's so scary.

26:28.503 --> 26:32.757
Your daughter-in-law is a cut above mine.

26:32.841 --> 26:34.968
If I'm the rabbit and you're the snake,

26:35.051 --> 26:37.304
then Ae-sun is a baby tiger.

26:37.387 --> 26:40.640
Come on, stop! I'm telling you.
You're not a rabbit either.

26:40.724 --> 26:42.642
Not all born
in the Year of the Rabbit are.

26:42.726 --> 26:45.520
Why aren't there years
of the raccoon, mole, or boar?

26:46.938 --> 26:49.316
What? List a few more, why don't you?

26:54.613 --> 26:55.447
Dad!

26:56.740 --> 26:57.657
Dear me.

26:58.658 --> 27:00.493
Hey. How was your day?

27:00.577 --> 27:01.661
Give this to Mom.

27:05.165 --> 27:06.666
What? What now?

27:07.250 --> 27:08.627
Is that how you say hello?

27:09.419 --> 27:12.797
Goodness. Why do you even have balls?

27:12.881 --> 27:15.133
They just make
sleeping on your belly awkward.

27:16.009 --> 27:18.720
Let's see.

27:19.220 --> 27:21.556
Did you tell Ae-sun…

27:22.265 --> 27:25.769
Did you make Ae-sun uncomfortable again?

27:25.852 --> 27:28.313
What about Gye-ok, then?

27:28.396 --> 27:30.649
Who's going to care if I'm uncomfortable?

27:30.732 --> 27:31.900
Your mom likes me.

27:32.692 --> 27:35.362
I gave birth to a son,
made you the captain,

27:35.445 --> 27:36.905
and gave her silver spoons.

27:37.489 --> 27:40.450
I gave her everything she wanted.

27:40.533 --> 27:42.702
She couldn't hate me
even if she wanted to.

27:42.786 --> 27:46.081
Wouldn't it be really strange
if she hated me?

27:48.124 --> 27:52.045
Your daughter-in-law
is indeed a cut above mine.

27:52.629 --> 27:54.923
I guess that means
my son is better than yours.

28:02.222 --> 28:05.392
Why would he give them
all three of the octopuses?

28:06.351 --> 28:08.353
What about our kids?

28:12.440 --> 28:13.608
Are you going?

28:14.234 --> 28:15.694
Are you going to your house?

28:16.486 --> 28:18.697
Yes, we are going.

28:19.989 --> 28:22.325
-We're moving to our house.
-All right.

28:23.576 --> 28:24.411
Go, then.

28:24.911 --> 28:26.329
I just wanted to say--

28:26.413 --> 28:28.373
Go! Go on your way!

28:29.541 --> 28:31.126
I really, really--

28:31.209 --> 28:32.419
Stop talking.

28:32.502 --> 28:34.671
Some things don't need to be said.

28:37.215 --> 28:38.049
Thank you.

28:38.133 --> 28:39.342
Crybaby mom!

28:40.051 --> 28:41.469
Pack your bags!

28:42.387 --> 28:43.847
Thank you for everything, sir.

28:45.473 --> 28:47.308
Go wake your little ones.

28:48.059 --> 28:49.894
We can't eat all of this by ourselves.

28:50.395 --> 28:52.772
We have to cook pork to celebrate.

28:52.856 --> 28:54.482
Why are we packing?

28:56.401 --> 28:58.486
They say hard times never last,

28:58.570 --> 29:02.240
but they lasted long enough for you,
living with your in-laws and then here,

29:03.283 --> 29:04.117
didn't they?

29:05.744 --> 29:07.620
Go live in your own house now.

29:36.149 --> 29:39.986
You said you'd been coming here alone
since you were six.

29:41.821 --> 29:45.992
You used to come over the hill
every chance you got.

29:53.458 --> 29:56.044
Mom!

29:57.086 --> 29:59.422
Mom!

30:01.674 --> 30:02.592
My baby!

30:03.301 --> 30:05.637
-You came over the hill alone again?
-Yeah!

30:05.720 --> 30:08.139
Oh my goodness!

30:09.599 --> 30:13.186
Mom!

30:13.686 --> 30:14.521
Oh dear.

30:14.604 --> 30:16.147
-Mom!
-Oh my, it's hot!

30:16.231 --> 30:18.441
Goodness, it's hot!

30:18.525 --> 30:20.318
It's so hot!

30:20.401 --> 30:21.277
It's hot!

30:21.361 --> 30:24.656
Mom, I made this. You like it?

30:24.739 --> 30:27.158
It's beautiful!

30:27.242 --> 30:30.161
My goodness, it's hot! Well done!

30:30.245 --> 30:32.622
Well done, my baby.

30:32.705 --> 30:33.790
Mom!

30:34.874 --> 30:37.752
Mom! I got a perfect score!

30:37.836 --> 30:40.046
My baby, it's freezing!

30:40.129 --> 30:42.715
How did you come over the hill
in this cold weather?

30:44.759 --> 30:46.010
SPELLING TEST

30:46.094 --> 30:48.096
-A perfect score.
-A perfect score.

30:48.179 --> 30:50.640
Well done. I'm so proud, my baby.

30:59.482 --> 31:02.026
You said you loved this house
because it was your mom's.

31:05.780 --> 31:09.826
You said you could smell her cooking
whenever you were here.

31:17.375 --> 31:22.255
You said your mother kept diving
for abalones to buy this house.

31:25.133 --> 31:26.301
We're not renting?

31:28.636 --> 31:31.014
No, I bought it.

31:31.764 --> 31:35.810
The landowner was from Busan,
so it was hard for him to manage anyway.

31:35.894 --> 31:37.395
It's not a lease?

31:39.898 --> 31:40.773
It's our home.

31:46.988 --> 31:49.157
It's the first time I've had my own home.

31:50.491 --> 31:51.910
Stupid home.

31:51.993 --> 31:55.663
Even conches and crabs have their own.

31:56.789 --> 32:01.210
But I was always the only one
without a home.

32:03.796 --> 32:05.006
My mom's house,

32:05.715 --> 32:07.216
my uncle's house,

32:08.343 --> 32:11.429
my stepdad's house,
and the one in Dodong-ri.

32:12.472 --> 32:14.515
None of them were my home.

32:15.808 --> 32:17.435
But this is actually…

32:18.227 --> 32:19.062
It's really…

32:22.607 --> 32:24.275
-Are you happy?
-Yes.

32:25.109 --> 32:26.027
I'm happy.

32:27.028 --> 32:27.987
Really.

32:29.113 --> 32:30.448
I'm so happy.

32:46.923 --> 32:49.676
I'll buy us a bigger house next time.

32:51.594 --> 32:53.429
This already feels like a palace.

32:54.973 --> 32:56.265
Now that it's my own,

32:57.892 --> 32:59.852
it feels even more like a palace.

33:04.023 --> 33:05.441
A little higher there.

33:06.234 --> 33:08.444
Summer somehow makes everything grow.

33:08.528 --> 33:09.362
Let me see.

33:09.445 --> 33:12.448
My diligent parents enjoyed
expanding our home so much

33:12.949 --> 33:17.078
that they didn't even notice
the sweat on their brows.

33:17.161 --> 33:18.287
Oh my!

33:18.371 --> 33:19.706
We should put one there too.

33:19.789 --> 33:21.916
Yes, there. Put another one there.

33:23.626 --> 33:26.337
Those are mother-of-pearls from Tongyeong.

33:26.421 --> 33:28.131
It's brand-new, not secondhand.

33:28.631 --> 33:30.383
It's brand-new, and it's all mine.

33:30.466 --> 33:31.676
It's really mine!

33:34.053 --> 33:36.931
Geum-myeong, do you want me
to pass it down to you later?

33:37.015 --> 33:39.267
Do you want it or not? You want it?

33:39.350 --> 33:40.435
Do you?

33:42.228 --> 33:43.479
Should we take a picture?

33:43.563 --> 33:46.774
It's not that big of a deal! Should we?

33:47.650 --> 33:48.484
Look.

33:48.568 --> 33:53.072
Many years later, even after moving
to an apartment with a built-in closet,

33:53.781 --> 33:57.410
Mom and Dad couldn't part
with the mother-of-pearl wardrobe.

33:58.619 --> 33:59.746
Let's go.

34:04.625 --> 34:06.627
The shiny pearl wardrobe

34:08.004 --> 34:11.758
reminded them
of their blazing summer days.

35:04.560 --> 35:06.145
The people who lived here before

35:06.229 --> 35:09.273
didn't take care of the place
because it wasn't theirs.

35:09.774 --> 35:13.820
They didn't even bother
to clean the hair out of the drain.

35:15.279 --> 35:16.364
Were you that busy?

35:18.407 --> 35:20.493
You never even appeared in my dream.

35:24.038 --> 35:25.790
Did you come because I bought a house?

35:26.958 --> 35:28.084
Because you're happy?

35:28.835 --> 35:30.169
Because you're proud?

35:31.420 --> 35:33.005
The woman next door bought a truck.

35:34.132 --> 35:34.966
What?

35:35.049 --> 35:38.261
Does he think being diligent at night
makes him a husband?

35:38.886 --> 35:42.056
You're full-term. Why is he always out
on the boat catching squid?

35:43.266 --> 35:45.643
Catching squid is how he bought the house.

35:45.726 --> 35:47.687
He should've bought a car already.

35:50.523 --> 35:53.442
Your neighbor
has a driver's license and a truck.

35:53.526 --> 35:55.987
You came here to talk about our neighbor?

35:56.070 --> 35:57.864
Are you jealous of her truck?

35:59.615 --> 36:03.035
It was hard enough to buy a house.
Why all the fuss about a car?

36:04.328 --> 36:08.166
If that persimmon tree reached
into our neighbor's house,

36:09.000 --> 36:10.293
then that woman…

36:12.378 --> 36:13.880
would eat all our persimmons.

36:14.839 --> 36:16.841
You should make her pay for eating them.

36:20.511 --> 36:21.554
Ae-sun.

36:22.638 --> 36:25.474
That woman has a truck.

36:29.896 --> 36:31.189
She has a truck.

36:45.077 --> 36:45.912
Geum-myeong.

36:48.497 --> 36:49.332
Geum-myeong.

36:51.792 --> 36:54.503
Go see the next-door neighbor now and…

37:33.209 --> 37:37.046
Let's have two kids and raise them well,
regardless of gender.

37:40.174 --> 37:45.263
My daughter-in-law only had two children,
but yours has won all three medals.

37:46.013 --> 37:49.100
The eldest is the gold medal
for being the breadwinner of this house.

37:49.183 --> 37:51.978
And the second and third are both sons.

37:52.061 --> 37:55.690
Your daughter-in-law
is indeed a cut above mine.

37:55.773 --> 37:58.901
She's way above! Far above!

38:00.319 --> 38:02.738
Didn't you say there was no son
in Ae-sun's fortune?

38:02.822 --> 38:05.658
An ancestor appeared in a dream
before his birth,

38:05.741 --> 38:08.244
so he will be a great blessing.

38:09.036 --> 38:10.079
Just wait and see.

38:10.162 --> 38:13.082
Gwan-sik will have full nets every day,

38:13.666 --> 38:16.585
thanks to this boy's maternal grandmother.

38:16.669 --> 38:19.380
You used to say
Ae-sun was bound to her mom's spirit.

38:19.463 --> 38:20.965
Now she is an ancestor?

38:21.048 --> 38:22.466
Even with any setbacks,

38:23.175 --> 38:26.554
this little one
is destined to thrive in life.

38:27.305 --> 38:30.057
You used to say
that Ae-sun's fortune had no blessings.

38:30.141 --> 38:31.642
You're such a…

38:33.561 --> 38:35.646
Such a what? A quack?

38:36.397 --> 38:38.232
I guess you can be spot-on sometimes.

38:42.153 --> 38:45.406
Full nets!

38:45.990 --> 38:49.452
Gwan-sik's boat has full nets again!

38:49.535 --> 38:51.078
Dong-myeong must be a blessing.

38:51.162 --> 38:53.414
Fish flock to the boat
whenever it sets sail.

38:53.497 --> 38:56.584
No, Ae-sun is the blessing.

38:56.667 --> 39:00.004
You see, I'm sure to make it
to a high position someday.

39:00.087 --> 39:01.088
You're right!

39:03.299 --> 39:06.594
The people's representative,
the worker for the people.

39:07.303 --> 39:09.680
Wait, no one was against it.

39:10.556 --> 39:11.974
Then it's basically unanimous.

39:12.058 --> 39:13.768
…for the presidential election.

39:13.851 --> 39:17.521
President Park Chung-hee,
the sole candidate,

39:17.605 --> 39:20.649
received 2,577 votes in favor
and one spoiled vote

39:20.733 --> 39:24.111
and was reelected as the president.

39:24.195 --> 39:26.697
I recommend Oh Ae-sun for deputy chief.

39:26.781 --> 39:27.782
Agreed!

39:27.865 --> 39:28.741
I second that!

39:28.824 --> 39:29.742
Me too!

39:29.825 --> 39:32.286
Stop it, everybody.

39:32.370 --> 39:34.830
I'm not interested in politics.

39:34.914 --> 39:36.540
Who's Oh Ae-sun?

39:36.624 --> 39:38.167
Gwang-rye's daughter.

39:38.250 --> 39:39.794
If she's Gwang-rye's daughter…

39:40.920 --> 39:42.880
…then let her do it!

39:44.173 --> 39:46.634
She was the class vice president
in school as well.

39:46.717 --> 39:48.135
Yes, vice president.

39:48.219 --> 39:51.180
Vetoed. I reject your request.

39:51.263 --> 39:53.140
The president picks his cabinet members.

39:53.224 --> 39:55.393
Why are you deciding who to appoint?

39:55.476 --> 39:58.896
Do you think a lion
would share a table with a hyena?

39:58.979 --> 40:02.858
Someone's on a power trip,
even though no one else ran.

40:02.942 --> 40:07.613
Even campaigns have
minimum requirements for candidacy.

40:07.696 --> 40:12.535
Can a dog and cow run for office?
Please just eat one, will you?

40:12.618 --> 40:13.661
But you have so many!

40:13.744 --> 40:16.080
Maybe I should run for chief.

40:16.163 --> 40:18.082
If a dog can run for it, why can't I?

40:23.212 --> 40:24.255
What, you brat?

40:24.338 --> 40:27.049
I'd rather not run for anything

40:27.550 --> 40:31.303
than hold a title with "deputy" in it.

40:31.804 --> 40:34.598
We didn't vote
because there was only one candidate,

40:34.682 --> 40:36.642
but if there are more, we should vote!

40:36.725 --> 40:38.144
-Vote!
-Vote!

40:38.227 --> 40:39.937
What have I got to lose?

40:40.020 --> 40:42.773
Let's just go head-to-head.

40:43.399 --> 40:44.817
Gwang-rye's daughter

40:44.900 --> 40:47.611
wants to go head-to-head with him!

40:47.695 --> 40:48.779
Goddamn it!

40:49.363 --> 40:50.656
A woman as the chief?

40:51.574 --> 40:53.659
What's wrong? Are you scared?

40:55.995 --> 40:57.163
Goddamn it!

40:59.081 --> 41:00.583
Goddamn it! Seriously?

41:00.666 --> 41:02.543
If you're not, let's vote.

41:02.626 --> 41:04.086
Hey, you little brat.

41:07.465 --> 41:08.924
Goddamn it! Hey!

41:10.009 --> 41:12.219
Huh?

41:12.303 --> 41:14.638
Just let her be the deputy chief.

41:14.722 --> 41:17.308
Don't embarrass yourself
by letting her run and win.

41:21.687 --> 41:25.191
I didn't know
she was this funny until today.

41:33.491 --> 41:35.993
A SMALL BALL LAUNCHED BY AE-SUN

41:36.076 --> 41:38.370
Ae-sun launched a small ball into the sky,

41:39.747 --> 41:42.917
and Dodong-ri got
its first female deputy chief.

41:43.584 --> 41:45.085
Hey, come on.

41:45.169 --> 41:46.795
Stop talking and look ahead.

41:47.296 --> 41:48.130
Look ahead.

41:48.214 --> 41:49.131
DEPUTY CHIEF

41:49.673 --> 41:51.509
Squeeze in, everyone.

41:52.301 --> 41:54.261
Shorter people to the front. Good.

41:54.345 --> 41:56.639
Move to the side. Come on, move along.

41:56.722 --> 41:57.598
One, two.

41:59.016 --> 42:01.977
Say "three" before taking pictures.
Has no one ever told you?

42:02.895 --> 42:05.189
All right. Everyone, look here.

42:05.272 --> 42:06.774
One, two, three.

42:10.069 --> 42:12.029
SOCIAL DANCE CLASS

42:12.112 --> 42:16.951
Hurry up! Come out now.
Stop resisting. Just come quickly.

42:21.997 --> 42:25.125
Come on! Take pictures!

42:25.209 --> 42:26.919
-What?
-Why are you taking pictures?

42:27.878 --> 42:29.296
Bring them all here.

42:30.756 --> 42:32.841
Quick. Come sit down.

42:32.925 --> 42:35.302
Gather them all like a pile of crap!
Get him!

42:36.845 --> 42:39.515
Aren't there more of them? Out of my way.

42:44.979 --> 42:47.231
Hey, is someone in there? Move aside.

42:49.316 --> 42:51.652
Why would you go in there, you creep?

42:51.735 --> 42:54.321
Creep?

42:55.030 --> 42:57.491
The ladies' room is my jurisdiction.

42:59.201 --> 43:03.247
Have you got a crush on me?
Why do you show up everywhere I go?

43:03.330 --> 43:07.167
Just go elsewhere, okay?
Go to a different area.

43:08.794 --> 43:11.171
What is it? You still think about me?

43:16.594 --> 43:17.428
Got any regrets?

43:28.564 --> 43:32.318
Hey, why are you pinching your nose?

43:33.068 --> 43:35.070
Why would you do that while I'm talking?

43:41.619 --> 43:42.536
Ma'am.

43:43.495 --> 43:44.747
It's all over.

43:44.830 --> 43:47.041
You're surrounded.

43:50.336 --> 43:52.212
Is someone in there or not?

44:03.891 --> 44:05.059
Those feet…

44:08.270 --> 44:10.147
The hell with socializing.

44:10.230 --> 44:12.941
When did we need dancing to socialize?

44:13.025 --> 44:16.153
The New Community Movement
made people too comfortable.

44:16.236 --> 44:17.655
All they want to do is party.

44:17.738 --> 44:20.115
No one would have done this
during the war.

44:20.199 --> 44:21.033
Go-go dancing?

44:21.617 --> 44:22.785
Social dancing?

44:22.868 --> 44:25.704
-We should send them to the 38th parallel.
-One, two.

44:26.413 --> 44:29.291
Count to three before you take pictures!

44:39.885 --> 44:40.886
Is this for real?

44:45.516 --> 44:46.600
Seriously!

44:46.684 --> 44:49.520
Why are you here? What do we do now?

44:51.772 --> 44:53.732
What now?

44:56.610 --> 44:58.445
Honestly.

45:05.661 --> 45:07.204
How do I get them out?

45:08.414 --> 45:09.456
Step aside.

45:16.839 --> 45:18.841
Cover your face with your clothes.

45:18.924 --> 45:21.009
You need to cover Hyeon-suk too!

45:23.762 --> 45:24.805
Good idea.

45:24.888 --> 45:26.849
Right? Look at these women.

45:26.932 --> 45:29.768
They eat well and have nothing to do,
so they dance around.

45:29.852 --> 45:30.978
I can't believe this.

45:31.061 --> 45:34.231
You have to go through a famine
to wake up to reality.

45:34.314 --> 45:36.567
Life must be good, right?

45:36.650 --> 45:38.235
Too good!

45:38.318 --> 45:40.362
Dance is a morally sound sport!

45:40.904 --> 45:42.114
-Hey!
-Well done.

45:42.698 --> 45:43.991
Morally sound, my foot!

45:44.575 --> 45:47.786
If that's true, why are you covering
your face with your clothes?

45:47.870 --> 45:49.747
Show your face and go to the Olympics.

45:49.830 --> 45:51.248
Win a medal and be a patriot.

45:51.331 --> 45:53.417
-Hyeon-suk, here.
-When hell freezes over!

45:53.500 --> 45:55.461
-One, two, three!
-You hear me?

45:55.961 --> 45:58.130
-One, two, three.
-Dance will never be a sport.

45:58.630 --> 46:00.299
Stop taking pictures!

46:07.765 --> 46:09.933
That woman is even carrying her child.

46:10.434 --> 46:12.561
She must be fleeing from the war.

46:13.103 --> 46:14.605
Take pictures of women like her!

46:14.688 --> 46:16.523
-Go get her.
-Get her!

46:17.441 --> 46:20.277
I'll get them!

46:25.991 --> 46:27.326
Stop right there!

46:29.369 --> 46:31.997
Why the hell
is she in my face all the time?

46:34.333 --> 46:36.001
She's doing better than you, Chief.

46:38.128 --> 46:41.381
All you know how to do
is count to three and take photos.

46:51.975 --> 46:56.104
You'll be on the news
for taking your child to the dance hall.

46:56.188 --> 46:58.148
Are you doing this because you're bored?

46:58.857 --> 47:00.651
Have you got too much money to spend?

47:00.734 --> 47:04.404
If I hadn't at least taken up jitterbug,
I would've gone mad.

47:05.280 --> 47:07.783
I would've killed myself or someone else.

47:11.161 --> 47:13.789
I feel rage inside when I'm stuck at home,

47:15.749 --> 47:18.585
but when I just hold hands
and spin around, it all goes away.

47:19.419 --> 47:22.381
So I can't help but go dancing.

47:25.926 --> 47:28.971
So, even at home, Chief is--

47:29.054 --> 47:31.014
He's still the same Shit-gil.

47:31.765 --> 47:33.809
My nickname at home is "Goddamn it!"

47:33.892 --> 47:34.810
Goddamn it!

47:36.144 --> 47:37.729
He's always saying, "Goddamn it,"

47:37.813 --> 47:42.109
so Hyeon-suk learned to say "Goddamn it"
before she could say "Dad."

47:42.901 --> 47:44.695
Mom, you're Cinderella.

47:47.906 --> 47:48.991
You're right.

47:49.074 --> 47:52.536
Cinderella left her shoe behind
after dancing and ran away.

48:00.460 --> 48:02.921
So that makes your dad the prince.

48:09.386 --> 48:10.470
These are better.

48:10.971 --> 48:13.765
You should wear something similar
to avoid his suspicion.

48:15.267 --> 48:16.143
Who knows?

48:16.810 --> 48:21.565
The prince of Dodong-ri might pick up
and bring a glass slipper.

48:22.149 --> 48:26.486
By the way, does your husband
really buy your hairpins for you?

48:26.987 --> 48:28.530
That's what everyone says.

48:29.531 --> 48:32.534
They say your husband catches fish
just to buy you hairpins.

48:34.620 --> 48:35.454
Seriously,

48:36.455 --> 48:39.917
people in this small town
are too interested in others' heads.

48:42.294 --> 48:44.087
Was that hairpin expensive?

48:44.671 --> 48:45.881
Ae-sun,

48:46.882 --> 48:48.717
you look more elegant than before.

48:49.509 --> 48:51.136
Like a noble person.

48:53.764 --> 48:54.890
I guess

48:56.516 --> 48:58.602
people look the way they live.

49:06.193 --> 49:07.027
Goddamn it!

49:10.322 --> 49:12.157
Just leave if you can't handle it.

49:12.240 --> 49:14.743
It's not like he's some great man
to look up to.

49:14.826 --> 49:16.620
Why live with your insides boiling?

49:18.538 --> 49:20.123
Is that why you turned him down?

49:20.749 --> 49:21.583
Sorry?

49:22.209 --> 49:25.087
You really don't have any regrets?

49:27.923 --> 49:31.760
Have you got a crush on me?
Why do you show up everywhere I go?

49:32.344 --> 49:35.847
Just go elsewhere, okay?
Go to a different area.

49:38.433 --> 49:41.353
What is it? You still think about me?

49:43.063 --> 49:44.064
Got any regrets?

49:46.566 --> 49:47.526
-Goodbye.
-Thank you.

49:49.027 --> 49:51.905
I have ears too, you know.
I know everything.

49:52.572 --> 49:55.909
I found out
you and my husband had a history.

49:58.745 --> 50:00.789
Come on, ma'am!

50:01.289 --> 50:03.083
What history?

50:03.166 --> 50:05.669
We just went on a blind date once.

50:06.169 --> 50:08.088
One blind date when I was young.

50:10.007 --> 50:13.719
Why just one date?
You should've spent more time with him.

50:15.053 --> 50:17.806
Then you might have ended up
in this pile of poop.

50:23.186 --> 50:26.189
Hyeon-suk, never step on a pile of poop.

50:26.773 --> 50:31.278
You have to marry a man
like this lady's husband, okay?

51:16.239 --> 51:17.949
Your handwriting is beautiful.

51:20.786 --> 51:22.621
The Literary Girl should do the writing.

51:34.883 --> 51:36.009
You want me on it?

51:36.927 --> 51:38.053
The paint will dry fast.

51:39.721 --> 51:41.848
It's bad luck for women to board the boat.

51:42.349 --> 51:43.934
The Dragon King might overturn it,

51:44.017 --> 51:45.310
and you won't make it back.

51:45.393 --> 51:47.395
-I don't believe in that stuff.
-Hey!

51:47.479 --> 51:48.980
Don't say that.

51:49.064 --> 51:52.109
The Dragon King and the gods
are all petty and hold grudges.

51:52.192 --> 51:53.485
I don't believe any of that.

51:54.194 --> 51:57.280
You, Geum-myeong, Eun-myeong,
and Dong-myeong are my gods.

51:57.781 --> 51:59.908
I'll survive a typhoon thanks to you four.

51:59.991 --> 52:01.451
I won't die no matter what.

52:01.952 --> 52:03.495
I'll always come back to you.

52:06.289 --> 52:07.249
I'll make it home.

52:12.379 --> 52:14.005
I know.

52:14.089 --> 52:15.257
You're our Steelheart.

52:17.384 --> 52:18.426
So get in.

52:19.344 --> 52:20.679
You're my blessing, right?

52:20.762 --> 52:24.099
You need to write it
for more fortune to come our way.

52:37.320 --> 52:40.949
Mom said she couldn't bring herself
to tell her daughter,

52:42.242 --> 52:45.287
"It's bad luck for you to board the boat."

52:49.416 --> 52:52.127
She didn't want to pass on
such a world to her daughter,

52:53.420 --> 52:56.631
so Mom flipped the table first.

53:42.636 --> 53:45.555
I never really believed
in the Dragon King anyway.

53:45.639 --> 53:47.140
I believe in myself!

53:47.224 --> 53:50.018
Why is it bad luck
for my little girl to board the boat?

53:51.061 --> 53:55.357
Do you even know
what's happening out here on land?

53:56.358 --> 53:58.818
You don't even know
the New Community Movement, gramps.

53:58.902 --> 54:01.738
Didn't you say the Dragon King
and the gods all hold grudges?

54:01.821 --> 54:03.740
Eun-myeong, Dong-myeong. Come here.

54:03.823 --> 54:05.909
I hold grudges too!

54:05.992 --> 54:09.663
Do you even know anything
about the Anti-superstition Movement?

54:10.247 --> 54:11.665
These days,

54:11.748 --> 54:14.793
the president is arresting people
for shamanistic rituals.

54:15.293 --> 54:16.795
If you get on my bad side,

54:16.878 --> 54:20.257
I won't even offer you a bowl of rice
on the ritual day!

54:21.383 --> 54:25.178
Why call me bad luck
when you feed off what I provide?

54:26.763 --> 54:28.974
You're such a strange old man!

54:29.683 --> 54:30.767
Spit at him. Spit.

54:35.897 --> 54:38.566
In the summer
that somehow makes everything grow,

54:38.650 --> 54:40.610
my young parents grew up too.

55:08.096 --> 55:09.597
GEUMEUNDONG

55:21.067 --> 55:24.529
Now we have a house

55:25.488 --> 55:26.823
and a boat.

55:28.033 --> 55:29.826
This is crazy.

55:31.411 --> 55:32.287
Are you happy?

55:33.455 --> 55:34.289
Yeah.

55:35.165 --> 55:35.999
I am happy.

55:38.251 --> 55:40.170
I'm so happy.

55:49.804 --> 55:52.098
With their lives full of catches,

55:53.016 --> 55:57.062
all they wanted was
for their blazing summer sunshine to last.

56:00.565 --> 56:01.941
They had no idea back then

56:02.942 --> 56:04.903
what else the summer could bring.

56:08.490 --> 56:09.866
FULL NETS

56:09.949 --> 56:14.496
A MIDSUMMER NIGHT'S FULL NETS

58:59.786 --> 59:04.624
"IN THE HOPE THAT OUR ECHOES
WILL FLOW AND FLOW UNTIL THEY REACH YOU."

59:12.048 --> 59:14.384
Subtitle translation by: Sung In Jang
